.TH NOSTR-HOMED-PROVISION-PUSH 1 "2026-09-25" "nostr-homed 0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nostr-homed-provision-push \- snapshot, encrypt and publish a portable-home tree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nostr-homed-provision push
\fB\-\-account\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR
[\fB\-\-home\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB\-\-chunk\-size\fR \fIBYTES\fR]
[\fB\-\-relay\fR \fIwss://...\fR]...
[\fB\-\-blossom\fR \fIhttps://...\fR]...
[\fB\-\-min\-replication\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-bump\-gen\fR]
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Snapshots a home tree, encrypts and uploads chunks to Blossom, and publishes
a new kind-30078 pointer. Reuses the exact
.I nh_syncd_push_batch
implementation that
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8)
runs internally, so a manual push produces a snapshot that is
bit-for-bit indistinguishable from a daemon push.
.PP
When a pointer already exists at the target d-tag, the caller MUST supply
.B \-\-bump\-gen
to publish a gen+1 pointer. Attempting to overwrite a pointer without a
generation bump is refused; the mistake is common enough that the CLI never
does it implicitly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-account\-file \fIPATH\fR
0600 account file. Required.
.TP
.B \-\-home \fIDIR\fR
Home tree to snapshot. Default:
.IR $HOME .
.TP
.B \-\-chunk\-size \fIBYTES\fR
Chunk size in bytes. Default 4 MiB. Clamped to the closed range [64 KiB, 8 MiB];
values outside that range are silently rounded to the nearest bound.
.TP
.B \-\-relay \fIwss://...\fR
Additional relay, appended to the account file for this push (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-blossom \fIhttps://...\fR
Additional Blossom server, appended to the account file for this push
(repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-min\-replication \fIN\fR
Refuse the push if fewer than N Blossom servers hold every chunk after
upload. Default 2. On failure, exit code is 77 and no pointer is published.
.TP
.B \-\-bump\-gen
Publish gen+1. Required when a pointer already exists.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a structured JSON summary on stdout (chunk hashes, per-server
replication table, pointer id) instead of the default text summary.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the planned manifest \(em chunk boundaries, hashes if the tree is
already ingested \(em and exit. No relay traffic, no Blossom upload.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT CODES
.RS
.TP 4
.B 0
Success (all chunks meet
.BR \-\-min\-replication ,
pointer published).
.TP 4
.B 2
Bad argument.
.TP 4
.B 71
Relay or Blossom transport failure.
.TP 4
.B 75
Cryptographic failure (encrypt, sign, or wrap).
.TP 4
.B 76
Internal error (I/O on the local tree, snapshot inconsistency).
.TP 4
.B 77
Insufficient replication \(em at least one chunk landed on fewer than
.B \-\-min\-replication
servers. Retry after the transient error clears; no pointer is published.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Routine daily push, requiring 2\-way replication:
.PP
.RS
.nf
nostr-homed-provision push \\
    \-\-account\-file ~/.config/nostr-homed/abcd1234.account.json \\
    \-\-bump\-gen
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview what would be uploaded, without touching the network:
.PP
.RS
.nf
nostr-homed-provision push \\
    \-\-account\-file ...account.json \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.PP
High\-replication push after adding a third Blossom mirror:
.PP
.RS
.nf
nostr-homed-provision push \\
    \-\-account\-file ...account.json \\
    \-\-blossom https://blossom-3.example \\
    \-\-min\-replication 3 \\
    \-\-bump\-gen \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <home>/.local/state/nostr-homed/porthome-status.json
Updated after every successful push; contains the new pointer id and
generation.
.SH SECURITY
The push path holds the account secret and derived home_key in memory. Both
are held in mlocked, secure-heap buffers and wiped before exit. The
account file mode is re-checked before each read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nostr-homed-provision (1),
.BR nostr-homed-provision-verify (1),
.BR nostr-home-syncd (8)
